🐛 Bug
This code pattern:
void errfail() {
 if(true)
  AT_ERROR("err");
 else
  AT_ERROR("false");
}

generates
fatal error: expected expression
on gcc & clang.
The workaround is to introduce braces, e.g.
 if(true) {
  AT_ERROR("err");
 } else {
  AT_ERROR("false");
 }

This error was not present in version 1.1.0 but I see it now from Tues (Jun 25) build.
